diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: IPv4 Neighbor/ARP reachability (NUD) on Linux L3 interfaces.
- Mechanism: All intermediate routers are aging their ARP/neighbor entries every 30 seconds (Linux default base_reachable_time_ms). When an entry goes STALE, the next packet triggers an ARP probe; during that probe initial packets are queued/dropped, briefly stalling the flow. Because your path crosses several L3 hops (r1 → r11 → r12), these 30 s refreshes sometimes align, compounding into a noticeable “freeze” that then clears—giving the impression the route is changing even though it is not.
